<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Özdemir Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Özdemir Pasha was an Ottoman commander of Circassian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> origin. As governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> he took Sanaa in 1547, and he then led the Ottoman advance on the African shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>, creating the province of Habesh in 1555 and seizing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massawa">Massawa</a> in 1557. He died in the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> in 1560; his son Özdemiroğlu Osman Pasha became grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ozdemir-pasha.jpg" alt="Özdemir Pasha" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Stanley from Nanaimo, Canada · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomb_of_Sheikh_Durbush_(8529063350).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
